1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Hello everyone, welcome to the quick tutorial series of Marlboro's Designer 2025.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
In this tutorial, we will introduce you to the view control method in Marlboro's Designer.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
First of all, you can go to the main menu, settings, user customization, and find the view control menu.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Select the preview of the operation method according to your needs.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
In the user preview download menu, select your usual operation method.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
You can choose according to the usual 3D software type or mouse type.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
In the view control column, you can also adjust and set certain operation methods separately.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,000
For example, in normal situations, when the mouse wheel rolls backwards, it pulls towards the camera.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
But if we move in the direction of the camera,

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
when the mouse wheel rolls backwards, it pulls towards the camera.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
You can save these settings as user customizations and use them later.

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
You can open the saved settings file in the user customizations.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Or you can directly reset the user customizations and restore the original settings.

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
In this series of tutorials, we use default settings.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Under default settings, press and hold the middle mouse button and drag the mouse button to parallel.

16
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Whether it is a 3D window or a 2D window, the operation method is the same.

17
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:46,000
When you move the mouse wheel, you can release the view.

18
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:53,000
At the same time, press and hold the left mouse button and drag the mouse button to release the view.

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The rotation view can only be done in the 3D window.

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Press and hold the right mouse button and drag the mouse button to rotate the view.

21
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
If we click on a certain object, it will automatically focus on this point.

22
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The rotation view is done in the focus position.

23
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Click on the 3D background again to cancel the focus mode.

24
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Click on the right mouse button and drag the mouse button to the 3D window.

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
There are also some view options in the 3D window.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
First is the correct and wrong view.

27
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
You can find and choose them here.

28
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
They all have corresponding small keyboard number shortcut keys.

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
For example, the correct view shortcut key is 2.

30
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Press the number key 2 to go back to the front view.

31
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
In addition, you can also choose to change the focal length.

32
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
This allows the 3D window to be adjusted so that you can see all visible objects.

33
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
This function is very useful for finding hidden objects.

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:07,000
The 2D window can also use the zoom in and out view function to find outside the field of view.

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:14,000
In addition, after selecting the field of view, press the shortcut key F to focus on the selected field of view.

36
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,000
In the 3D window, you can also focus on the selected field of view.

37
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:24,000
After that, the zoom in and out view is also done by focusing on objects.

38
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
This is the tutorial for trying to control.

39
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,000
See you in the next video.

